2025-05-26 22:32:10,609 - agentpress - INFO - response_processor.py:1074 - Tool execution complete: scrape_webpage -> ToolResult(success=True, output='[\n  {\n    "Title": "n8n\'s 2024 in Review \\u2013 n8n Blog",\n    "URL": "https://blog.n8n.io/2024-in-review/",\n    "Text": "We use analytics\\n\\nWe use cookies and other tracking technologies to improve your browsing experience, to analyze our website\\ntraffic, assist our marketing efforts and to understand where our visitors are coming from.\\n\\n\\n[Privacy Policy](https://n8n.io/legal#privacy)\\n\\nDecline\\nAgree\\n\\n![2024 in Review](https://blog.n8n.io/content/images/size/w1600/2025/01/2024-review-v2.png)\\n\\n[News](https://blog.n8n.io/tag/news/)\\n\\n# 2024 in Review\\n\\nAs we dive into 2025, we\'re taking a moment to reflect on our achievements throughout 2024. We\'ve grown a lot as a team, as a global community, and as a product, and we\'ve done more than we can possibly share in one blogpost. We\\u2019ll try though! Here\'s an overview of our highlights.\\n\\n\\n[![Bart Veldhuizen](https://blog.n8n.io/content/images/size/w120/2024/06/Le-Moi-square.jpg)](https://blog.n8n.io/author/bart/)\\n\\n[Bart Veldhuizen](https://blog.n8n.io/author/bart/)\\n\\nJanuary 21, 2025 \\u2219 4 minutes read\\n\\n\\n### Building an amazing team\\n\\n![](https://blog.n8n.io/content/images/2025/01/n8n-Tuscany-IRL.png)\\n\\nAt n8n we put a **lot** of effort into building a great team with a great culture. And as we grew from 37 to 71 team members, the team spirit and the love for n8n remained intact. One of the \\u2018team culture\\u2019 things we love doing is getting the entire company together twice a year. This year, we met in Berlin and Tuscany for three days of strategising and team building.\\n\\n![](https://blog.n8n.io/content/images/2025/01/Team-growth.jpg)\\n\\n2025 will be another year of strong team growth. Do you think n8n is the right place for you? Join us \\u2013 [We\\u2019re hiring](https://n8n.io/careers?ref=blog.n8n.io)!\\n\\n### Empowering automation with AI\\n\\nAI took center stage in our 2024 product development. The marriage of n8n\'s \'traditional\' workflow automation tools with LLMs, Vector Stores, Agents, and Tools has proven to be extremely successful, unlocking powerful automations with relative ease.\\n\\nWe rolled out a wide range of new AI features that make workflows smarter, faster, and more efficient:\\n\\n- **Chat Trigger**: Improved canvas chat and far better logging, allowing for more insight into the information flow between components.\\n- **New AI Models**: Expanded support to include Claude, Gemini, Groq, and Vertex models, giving users greater flexibility.\\n- **External Vector Stores**: Integration with more external vector stores opened new possibilities for working with large datasets.\\n- **AI Nodes**: New tools like the AI Transform Node and AI App Tools made it easier to process, generate, and analyze data.\\n- **AI Agents**: AI Agents enabled workflows to operate autonomously, taking automation to the next level.\\n\\nWe also launched the [Self-Hosted AI Starter Kit](https://docs.n8n.io/hosting/starter-kits/ai-starter-kit/?ref=blog.n8n.io), allowing teams to run their AI workflows and LLMs on their own infrastructure and to keep their data private.\\n\\nCurious to learn more? [Check out this new video series by our DevRel Max](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yzvLfHb0nqE&ref=blog.n8n.io) where he dives into every aspect of AI in n8n.\\n\\n![](https://blog.n8n.io/content/images/2025/01/YouTube---Building-AI-Agents-with-Max.png)\\n\\n### Creating a smoother, more powerful platform\\n\\nWe made many improvements to the n8n platform. Some are obvious, but others are harder to spot, and ensure n8n remains a powerful and performant tool in 2025 and beyond:\\n\\n- **Overhauled Expression Editor**: The revamped editor, paired with new [data transformation functions](https://docs.n8n.io/release-notes/?ref=blog.n8n.io#new-data-transformation-functions), simplifies complex data manipulations. We added context-aware code completion to make it much easier to get started with expressions.\\n- **Dark Mode + Dark Nodes**: A long-awaited visual update that removes the need for wearing sunglasses during your nightly n8n sessions.\\n- **New Canvas:** Our new, more performant canvas is almost out of beta! We redid the entire implementation to make it easier to work with large workflows and large datasets (stay tuned for more!).\\n- **Task Runners for Code Node:** Also still in beta, Task Runners will add up to a 6x performance boost to your Javascript Code Nodes!\\n\\n![](https://blog.n8n.io/content/images/2025/01/Pull-request-2.jpg)\\n\\n### Adding more power with more nodes\\n\\n2024 also saw the addition of **tons of new nodes** to extend n8n\\u2019s capabilities and integrate with even more tools.\\n\\nOne stand-out addition is the new [Form Trigger Node](https://docs.n8n.io/integrations/builtin/core-nodes/n8n-nodes-base.formtrigger/?ref=blog.n8n.io) that allows for building interactive workflows with multi-step forms that collect data seamlessly. We also added nodes for popular applications like MS OneDrive, Google Business, Okta and Gong. And what\\u2019s a workflow without a trigger? We now also have triggers for MS OutLook, Salesforce, Slack, Whatsapp, Twilio and more!\\n\\nYou can find all our nodes on our [integrations page](https://n8n.io/integrations/?ref=blog.n8n.io).\\n\\n![](https://blog.n8n.io/content/images/2025/01/Versions.jpg)\\n\\n### A growing, vibrant community\\n\\n2024 was also the year that we were able to invest a lot of time into you, our amazing community! Here are some of the things we achieved together:\\n\\n- We restructured our [community forum](https://community.n8n.io/?ref=blog.n8n.io) \\u2013 still the best place to get help with n8n.\\n- Stepped up our activity on [YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/n8n-io?ref=blog.n8n.io), including Max\\u2019 amazing [30 days of AI](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Jgouaas1fUE&list=PLlET0GsrLUL7Ja8Hv6Ra6bdBHENj-ODwF&ref=blog.n8n.io) and his new series, [the Studio](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OSVZfSDyaYM&list=PLlET0GsrLUL7LWMf4Q3gHNu5mk-hur7QV&ref=blog.n8n.io). Also, Angel has started a new series for Enterprise and IT users called [n8n at Scale](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WneT4gliSbY&ref=blog.n8n.io). Check it out!\\n- We restarted our monthly Community Hangouts - livestreams where we talk about what\\u2019s going on at n8n, and where we invite speakers from our community. In December, we also interviewed our founder Jan Oberhauser and we celebrated the 2024 Community Awards! [You can see the episode here.](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=64bCy3vVSxw&t=2454s&ref=blog.n8n.io)\\n- We launched our [Community Newsletter](https://n8n.io/newsletter?ref=blog.n8n.io) \\u2013 a monthly summary of product updates, featured templates and community activities.\\n- We started an Ambassador program. We welcomed 19 Ambassadors, who already [hosted 14 events](https://community.n8n.io/tag/meetup-report?ref=blog.n8n.io) around the world.\\n- Finally, our social media is more active than ever! Follow us on [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/company/n8n/?ref=blog.n8n.io), [X](https://x.com/n8n_io?ref=blog.n8n.io), [Facebook](https://www.facebook.com/n8nio/) or [Bluesky](https://bsky.app/profile/n8n.io?ref=blog.n8n.io) to stay up to date on feature updates, community events, great educational videos and more!\\n\\n![](https://blog.n8n.io/content/images/2025/01/community-collage.png)![](https://blog.n8n.io/content/images/2025/01/Community-authored-2.jpg)\\n\\n### Onward to 2025\\n\\nWe\\u2019re all excited for the future of n8n! Whether it\\u2019s advancing AI, improving workflows, or growing alongside our community, we\\u2019re committed to making automation more accessible, powerful, and user-friendly.\\n\\nTo learn more about our plans, [join our next Community Livestream on January 30](https://lu.ma/n8n-january-2025?ref=blog.n8n.io), where our Product Managers will unfold their plans.\\n\\nThank you for being part of this journey \\u2013 here\\u2019s to an even more exciting year ahead!\\n\\n## Subscribe to n8n newsletter\\n\\nGet the best, coolest, and latest in automation and low-code delivered to your inbox each week.\\n\\n\\n[iframe](https://www.google.com/recaptcha/api2/anchor?ar=1&k=6LeAQeopAAAAAKlLsRb1weWm6T_vijoQBkGkbHzB&co=aHR0cHM6Ly9ibG9nLm44bi5pbzo0NDM.&hl=en&v=jt8Oh2-Ue1u7nEbJQUIdocyd&size=invisible&cb=bulcmywyd4cc)\\n\\nSomething went wrong. Please try again later.\\n\\nSubscribed!\\n\\nSubscrib\\n...\\n[Content truncated due to length limit]",\n    "Metadata": {\n      "description": "As we dive into 2025, we wanted to take a moment to reflect on our achievements throughout 2024.",\n      "og:image": "https://blog.n8n.io/content/images/size/w1200/2025/01/2024-review-v2.png",\n      "twitter:data1": "Bart Veldhuizen",\n      "ogImage": "https://blog.n8n.io/content/images/size/w1200/2025/01/2024-review-v2.png",\n      "HandheldFriendly": "True",\n      "ogDescription": "As we dive into 2025, we\'re taking a moment to reflect on our achievements throughout 2024. We\'ve grown a lot as a team, as a global community, and as a product, and we\'ve done more than we can possibly share in one blogpost. We\\u2019ll try though! Here\'s an overview of our highlights.",\n      "generator": "Ghost 5.120",\n      "og:type": "article",\n      "ogTitle": "n8n\'s 2024 in Review",\n      "og:description": "As we dive into 2025, we\'re taking a moment to reflect on our achievements throughout 2024. We\'ve grown a lot as a team, as a global community, and as a product, and we\'ve done more than we can possibly share in one blogpost. We\\u2019ll try though! Here\'s an overview of our highlights.",\n      "language": "en",\n      "modifiedTime": "2025-01-23T15:51:15.000Z",\n      "og:title": "n8n\'s 2024 in Review",\n      "article:tag": "News",\n      "twitter:data2": "News",\n      "twitter:label2": "Filed under",\n      "viewport": "width=device-width, initial-scale=1",\n      "article:published_time": "2025-01-21T12:32:38.000Z",\n      "twitter:site": "@n8n_io",\n      "ogUrl": "https://blog.n8n.io/2024-in-review/",\n      "publishedTime": "2025-01-21T12:32:38.000Z",\n      "twitter:description": "As we dive into 2025, we\'re taking a moment to reflect on our achievements throughout 2024. We\'ve grown a lot as a team, as a global community, and as a product, and we\'ve done more than we can possibly share in one blogpost. We\\u2019ll try though! Here\'s an overview of our highlights.",\n      "title": "n8n\'s 2024 in Review \\u2013 n8n Blog",\n      "og:url": "https://blog.n8n.io/2024-in-review/",\n      "og:image:height": "677",\n      "twitter:card": "summary_large_image",\n      "twitter:label1": "Written by",\n      "favicon": "https://blog.n8n.io/content/images/size/w256h256/2022/06/logo-n8n-symbol-512x512.png",\n      "article:publisher": "https://www.facebook.com/n8nio",\n      "twitter:image": "https://blog.n8n.io/content/images/size/w1200/2025/01/2024-review-v2.png",\n      "twitter:url": "https://blog.n8n.io/2024-in-review/",\n      "og:site_name": "n8n Blog",\n      "article:modified_time": "2025-01-23T15:51:15.000Z",\n      "og:image:width": "1200",\n      "twitter:title": "n8n\'s 2024 in Review",\n      "referrer": "no-referrer-when-downgrade",\n      "ogSiteName": "n8n Blog",\n      "scrapeId": "ddd02145-5cc6-4f9d-97b8-172313eab427",\n      "sourceURL": "https://blog.n8n.io/2024-in-review/",\n      "url": "https://blog.n8n.io/2024-in-review/",\n      "statusCode": 200,\n      "proxyUsed": "basic"\n    }\n  }\n]')
